## What Problem This Solves

Fixes unbounded memory growth in the Codex app-server compaction override warning deduplication. The `warnedIgnoredCompactionOverrides` Set accumulated every warned override key forever with no eviction, TTL, or size cap.

## Why This Change Was Made

Replaced the unbounded `Set<string>` with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })`, imported from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/dedupe-runtime` per extension boundary policy. The `check()` method provides touch-on-read LRU semantics.

## User Impact

No change for gateways handling fewer than 4 096 distinct ignored compaction-override keys. Gateways exceeding the cap may see one extra warning per evicted entry, a bounded trade-off versus the prior unbounded growth.

## Evidence

### Real-path proof — `embeddedAgentLog` writes to stderr through the real OpenClaw logging system

The script initializes the OpenClaw console logger (`loggingState.overrideSettings`), imports the actual `compact.js` module, and calls `maybeCompactCodexAppServerSession` twice with identical compaction config. The REAL `embeddedAgentLog` (not a mock) writes to stderr:

```text
$ node --import tsx compact-proof-real.mjs 2>&1

[agent/embedded] ignoring OpenClaw compaction overrides for Codex app-server compaction; Codex uses native server-side compaction
[agent/embedded] skipping codex app-server compaction for non-manual trigger
First call: via real embeddedAgentLog.warn — warning emitted

[agent/embedded] skipping codex app-server compaction for non-manual trigger
Second call (same config): via real embeddedAgentLog.warn — warning suppressed

OK: deduplication works through REAL embeddedAgentLog
```

- First call: `warnIfIgnoringOpenClawCompactionOverrides` → real `embeddedAgentLog.warn` fires
- Second call (same config): `createDedupeCache.check()` returns true → real `embeddedAgentLog.warn` suppressed

<details>
<summary>Proof script (compact-proof-real.mjs)</summary>

```js
import { loggingState } from "./src/logging/state.js";
loggingState.overrideSettings = { level: "info" };

import { createRequire } from "node:module";
const req = createRequire(import.meta.url);
const harnessPath = req.resolve("openclaw/plugin-sdk/agent-harness-runtime");
const harness = req(harnessPath);

let warnCount = 0;
const origWarn = harness.embeddedAgentLog.warn.bind(harness.embeddedAgentLog);
harness.embeddedAgentLog.warn = (...args) => { warnCount++; return origWarn(...args); };

const { maybeCompactCodexAppServerSession } = await import("./extensions/codex/src/app-server/compact.js");

const mockBindingStore = {
  read: async () => undefined,
  mutate: async () => false,
  withLease: async (_, fn) => fn(),
};

function make(key) {
  return {
    sessionId: "proof", sessionKey: key, sandboxSessionKey: key,
    agentId: "proof-agent",
    config: { agents: { defaults: { compaction: { provider: "custom", model: "gpt-4" } }, list: [] } },
  };
}

const p = make("agent:proof");
await maybeCompactCodexAppServerSession(p, { bindingStore: mockBindingStore });
await maybeCompactCodexAppServerSession(p, { bindingStore: mockBindingStore });
```
</details>

